[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: People and permissions
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Users, profiles and who may manage or complete what. UIDs: REQ-BE-020 .. 029.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-020
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: User management
STATEMENT: >>>
An administrator shall be able to create, edit, reorder and delete people, and set per person whether they can log in and whether they are an administrator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-021
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Agenda managers
STATEMENT: >>>
Each person shall have a list of people who may manage their agenda, by default the person themself. Only those people shall be able to create, edit or delete that person's agenda items.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-022
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Task managers
STATEMENT: >>>
The task system shall be enabled per person, with a list of people who may manage that person's tasks. Only those people shall be able to create, edit, move, reorder or delete that person's tasks. Completing tasks follows REQ-BE-024.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-023
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Own profile
STATEMENT: >>>
A logged-in user shall be able to change their own name, e-mail address, password and profile colour.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Who may complete tasks
STATEMENT: >>>
A task occurrence shall be marked as done only when requested by the person the task belongs to, by one of that person's task managers, by an administrator, or by a device logged in as a wall tablet. Other requests shall get HTTP 403 with a Dutch error message.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Children tick off their own tasks on their phone or on the shared wall tablet without needing rights to change them.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
'Logged in as a wall tablet' means the token was issued with device type 'dashboard' (REQ-BE-012). The device type is declared by the client at login.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-022
